-- title:
--   Equal floor readings and supersingular fibre force equal Γ₀(M')-class
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $q\ge 5$ and $M'$ is a non-zero natural number with $q\nmid M'$. Further, $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}=\mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\ \mathbb Q$ satisfying `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$; $W$ is a finite set of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,M'$ over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ whose members are, by `hW`, exactly the places in `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`, that is the places satisfying the predicate `IsSupersingularPlace q M'`; and $s$ is one element of $W$. Here $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,K\,N$ is the subfield of $K((\mathsf q))$ generated over $K$ by the two series $j(\mathsf q)$ and $j(\mathsf q^{N})$. The hypothesis `hle` asserts that $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$, the subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((\mathsf q))$ generated over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ by the coefficientwise images of the full level-$M'$ modular function field $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFull}\,M'\subset\mathbb Q((\mathsf q))$, is contained in `fieldBar q M'`, the field attached to the level $q^2M'$ and to the subgroup $\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M'=\ker\big((\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times\big)$ of units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$.
--
--   The datum $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ from $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ to $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,M'$: a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ of the source, a surjective ring homomorphism $R_0.\mathrm{residue}$ from it onto the target whose kernel is the maximal ideal, a map $R_0.\mathrm{placeMap}$ on places, subject to the clauses of the structure (membership in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ of a constant is membership in $A$; compatibility of $R_0.\mathrm{residue}$ with the residue map of $A$ on constants; every non-zero element can be scaled by a constant into $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ with non-zero residue; $R_0.\mathrm{placeMap}$ preserves degrees and pushes forward the divisor of a function with non-zero residue to the divisor of the residue). The hypothesis `hR₀` couples $R_0$ with coefficientwise reduction: for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}((\mathsf q))$ lies in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$, that element belongs to $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, is the series obtained from $y$ by applying $\mathrm{residue}_A$ to each coefficient.
--
--   The field of constants is an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\mathbb Q\subset\overline{\mathbb Q}$; write $A_0=A\cap k_0$ for $A.\mathrm{comap}$ of the structure map $k_0\to\overline{\mathbb Q}$, and $\kappa=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A_0$. An element $\pi_0\in k_0$ is given with $\pi_0\in A$, and the hypotheses on $A_0$ are: $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`) whose maximal ideal is generated by $\pi_0$ (`hunif`), $A_0$ is a henselian local ring (`hhens`), $\kappa$ is algebraically closed (`hres`), and (`hκ`) every element of $A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0$ lying in $A$.
--
--   The auxiliary prime is $\ell'$, with $\ell'\neq q$, $\ell'\ge 3$ and $\ell'\nmid M'$. An element $\xi\in k_0$ is a primitive $(q\ell')$-th root of unity (`hξ`), and `hιξ` posits a ring homomorphism $k_0\to\mathbb C$ carrying $\xi$ to $\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell'))$. The field $K$ is an intermediate field of $k_0\subset k_0((\mathsf q))$ which by `hK` equals $\mathrm{laurentBaseChange}\,k_0$ of $\mathrm{xHFunctionField}\,((q\ell')^2M')\,(\mathrm{levelH}\,(q\ell')\,M')$, i.e. the subfield of $k_0((\mathsf q))$ generated over $k_0$ by the coefficientwise images of the rational function field of level $(q\ell')^2M'$ with group the kernel of $(\mathbb Z/(q\ell')^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q\ell')^\times$; $K$ is an $A_0$-algebra, compatibly with $A_0\to k_0\to K$. Finally $j$ is a non-zero element of $K$ whose image in $k_0((\mathsf q))$ is the coefficientwise image of $\mathrm{jq}=\mathsf q^{-1}\cdot\mathrm{jNumQ}$, the $\mathsf q$-expansion of the modular $j$-function.
--
--   Four groups of functoriality hypotheses are imposed, all quantified over $A_0$-algebras. `hℓ` states that level-$P$ structures at $\ell'$ are preserved by variable change: for a Weierstrass curve $W$ over $T$, a variable change $C$ and level-$P$ data $D$, $\mathrm{IsLevelPStructure}\,W\,\ell'\,D$ implies $\mathrm{IsLevelPStructure}\,(C\bullet W)\,\ell'\,(D.\mathrm{variableChange}\,C)$. `hM` states the corresponding equivariance of the predicate $\mathrm{IsGamma0PowAt}\,W\,p\,k\,h$ under replacing $h$ by $\mathrm{kernelVariableChangeDeg}\,C\,(\mathrm{gamma0PowDeg}\,p\,k)\,h$. The group-law data consist of $\mathcal G:\mathrm{GroupLaws}\,A_0$, assumed chord-and-tangent (`h𝒢`: each relative group law is the one computed by a points-evaluation) and origin-normalised (`h𝒢O`: the identity section is cut out by a homomorphism from the origin chart ring killing $x/y$ and $z/y$), together with a level transport $\mathcal T:\mathrm{LevelTransport}\,A_0\,\mathcal G\,q$ satisfying `h𝒯`, the section-transport property (the transported Drinfeld pair has the expected curve and its two sections pull back along variable-change and coefficient-change homomorphisms of graded Proj models to the original ones). Finally `hVC` and `hCO` provide, for every projective Weierstrass curve over an $A_0$-algebra, a graded ring homomorphism of its Proj model grading realising a given variable change, respectively a given $A_0$-algebra map of coefficients, in each case with the irrelevant ideal of the target contained in the image of the irrelevant ideal of the source, and satisfying $\mathrm{IsVariableChangeHom}$, respectively $\mathrm{IsCoefficientHom}$.
--
--   Let $\mathcal R=\mathrm{rigidDataPow}\,A_0\,\ell'\,M'\,q\,\mathrm{h}\ell\,\mathrm{hM}\,\mathcal G\,\mathcal T$ be the rigid Weierstrass data obtained from the product of the $\Gamma_0(p^k)$-component for $M'$, the level-$P$ component at $\ell'$ and the Drinfeld level component at $q$. Then $P_0$ is a `LevelModuliPackageAbs` for $\mathcal R.\mathrm{toLevelModuliDatum}$: an $A_0$-algebra $P_0.B_0$ with a point $P_0.\mathrm{univ}$ over it such that every point over an $A_0$-algebra $T$ is the image of $P_0.\mathrm{univ}$ under a unique $A_0$-algebra map $P_0.B_0\to T$. A point $x_0$ of $\mathcal R.\mathrm{toLevelModuliDatum}$ over $K$ is given whose $j$-invariant equals, in $k_0((\mathsf q))$, the series $\mathrm{jqNModC}\,k_0\,(q\ell')=j(\mathsf q^{q\ell'})$ (`hx₀`), and $\mathrm{clC}$ is an $A_0$-algebra map from $P_0.B_0$ to the chart algebra $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A_0\,K\,j$ (the finite chart of the two-chart integral model determined by $j$) whose composite with the inclusion into $K$ is the classifying map $P_0.\mathrm{classify}\,x_0$ (`hclC`).
--
--   The hypothesis `hμ` pins $x_0$ to the Tate curve: there are a variable change $C$ over $k_0((\mathsf q))$ and a raw point $r$ of $\mathcal R$ over $K$ with $\mathrm{Quot.mk}\,r=x_0$, such that (i) writing $(\mathrm x,\mathrm y)=\mathrm{cuspPoint}\,k_0\,(q\ell')\,\xi\,[1,0]$ one has $C.u\cdot(2\mathrm x+1/6)=2\mathrm y+\mathrm x$, $C.r=-1/12$, $C.s=-1/2$, $C.t=1/24$ (the last three as constant Laurent series); (ii) the curve of $r$, pushed to $k_0((\mathsf q))$, equals $C\bullet\mathrm{tateBase}\,k_0\,(q\ell')$; (iii) for every prime $p\mid M'$, every field $F'$, every ring homomorphism $f:k_0\to F'$ and every primitive $p^{v_p(M')}$-th root of unity $\zeta\in F'$, the $\Gamma_0$-component polynomial $r.\mathrm{level}.1\,p$, pushed to $F'((\mathsf q))$ via $f$, equals $\mathrm{kernelVariableChangeDeg}$ of $C$ (pushed by $f$) in degree $\mathrm{gamma0PowDeg}\,p\,v_p(M')$ applied to $\prod_{1\le a\le p^{v_p(M')}/2,\;p\nmid a}\big(X-(\mathrm{toricPoint}\,F'\,(q\ell')\,\zeta^a).1\big)$; (iv) the level-$P$ datum $r.\mathrm{level}.2.1$, pushed to $k_0((\mathsf q))$, equals $(\mathrm{cuspData}\,k_0\,(q\ell')\,\xi\,[q,0]\,[0,-q]).\mathrm{variableChange}\,C$; and (v) there are $P_x,P_y,Q_x,Q_y\in K$ whose images in $k_0((\mathsf q))$ are the four coordinates $\mathrm{xP},\mathrm{yP},\mathrm{xQ},\mathrm{yQ}$ of $(\mathrm{cuspData}\,k_0\,(q\ell')\,\xi\,[\ell',0]\,[0,-\ell']).\mathrm{variableChange}\,C$, and the two Drinfeld sections satisfy $\mathrm{IsSectionThrough}\,(r.\mathrm{level}.2.2.P)\,P_x\,P_y$ and $\mathrm{IsSectionThrough}\,(r.\mathrm{level}.2.2.Q)\,Q_x\,Q_y$, i.e. each is cut out by a homomorphism from the $Z$-chart ring with the given affine coordinates.
--
--   Under these hypotheses the assertion is the following. Let $y,y'$ be maximal ideals of the chart algebra $\mathcal C=\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A_0\,K\,j$ and let $\psi,\psi':\mathcal C\to\kappa$ be $A_0$-algebra maps with $\psi(c)=0\iff c\in y$ and $\psi'(c)=0\iff c\in y'$. Assume the floor readings of $\psi$ and $\psi'$ agree, in the following sense: for every $g\in\mathbb Q((\mathsf q))$ lying in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFull}\,M'$ whose coefficientwise image in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, such that $g$ is cusp-regular relative to $j$ (for every place $P$ of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, $0\le P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the image of $\mathrm{jq}$ implies $0\le P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the image of $g$) and such that the $R_0$-residue of $g$ lies in the valuation subring of the place $s$, and for any proofs that $\mathrm{qExpand}\,k_0\,\ell'(\mathrm{coeffEmb}\,k_0\,g)=g(\mathsf q^{\ell'})$ lies in $K$ and in $\mathcal C$, the values of $\psi$ and $\psi'$ on that element of $\mathcal C$ coincide.
--
--   Then, for all raw points $x,x'$ of $\mathcal R$ over $\kappa$ such that the class of $x$ in $\mathcal R.\mathrm{Pt}\,\kappa$ is the image of $P_0.\mathrm{univ}$ under $\psi\circ\mathrm{clC}$ and the class of $x'$ is the image of $P_0.\mathrm{univ}$ under $\psi'\circ\mathrm{clC}$, assuming that the affine curve of $x$ has no non-zero $\kappa$-point killed by $q$ (every $P$ with $q\cdot P=0$ is $0$), and for all points $g$ of the affine curve of $x$ and $g'$ of the affine curve of $x'$ such that $g$ has additive order $M'$ and is cut out by the $\Gamma_0$-component of $x$ — for every prime $p\mid M'$, every $n$ and every non-singular affine point $(x_1,y_1)$ with $n\cdot g=(x_1,y_1)$ and $\mathrm{addOrderOf}(n\cdot g)=p^{v_p(M')}$, the polynomial $x.\mathrm{level}.1\,p$ vanishes at $x_1$ — and such that $g'$ satisfies the same two conditions with respect to $x'$, the two $\Gamma_0(M')$-pairs agree in $\mathrm{ModuliPoint}\,M'\,\kappa$:
--   $$\big[\,(x.\mathrm{curve},\,g)\,\big]=\big[\,(x'.\mathrm{curve},\,g')\,\big],$$
--   the elliptic structures being supplied by the invertibility of the discriminants of $x.\mathrm{curve}$ and $x'.\mathrm{curve}$, and the classes being taken in the quotient of $\mathrm{Gamma0Pair}\,M'\,\kappa$ by the relation $\mathrm{Gamma0Pair.Step}$.
--
--   This is the geometric core of the constancy argument for the supersingular fibre: two closed points of the finite chart of the integral model of $K$ at which all admissible level-$M'$ functions read the same value, and which lie over the chosen supersingular place $s$, carry the same $\Gamma_0(M')$-moduli class over the algebraically closed residue field $\kappa$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_place_forall_isModuliPlaceOf_of_over_of_eq_map_classify_rigidDataPow_of_tatePoint`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_place_forall_isModuliPlaceOf_of_over_of_eq_map_classify_rigidDataPow_of_tatePoint).
